00:04:22,105 --> 00:04:28,105
They don't belong here.

2
00:08:44,210 --> 00:08:50,210
White Settlers is a mystery, thriller, horror film directed by Simeon Halligan.

3
00:13:06,315 --> 00:13:12,315
Young urban couple Ed and Sarah are set to begin a new life when they move
from London into an isolated borders Scottish farmhouse.

4
00:17:28,421 --> 00:17:34,421
After falling in love with the 19th century Castle Farm and seeing its potential as
a fixer-upper they are anxious to get started on the renovations.

5
00:21:50,526 --> 00:21:56,526
In bed on their first night Sarah thinks she can hear noises in the darkness but
Ed is disbelieving saying it’s her imagination playing tricks.

6
00:26:12,631 --> 00:26:18,631
Persisting in her fear they are not alone in the
house, she forces Ed to investigate.

7
00:30:34,736 --> 00:30:40,736
When he doesn’t return after a scarily long period, she goes downstairs to investigate
only to be confronted by a welcoming committee of masked intruders.

8
00:34:56,842 --> 00:35:02,842
As she desperately searches for Ed, a terrifying game of cat
and mouse ensues with the mysterious assailants.

9
00:39:18,947 --> 00:39:24,947
But what do they want and what horrors do they
have planned for the two newcomers?

10
00:43:41,052 --> 00:43:47,052
Sarah, played by Pollyanna McIntosh.

11
00:48:03,157 --> 00:48:09,157
Ed, played by Lee Williams.

12
